sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant E as eUICC (ISD-R / ECASD)
    participant L as LPA (OpenEUICC)
    participant S as SM-DP+ server

    Note over E: Trust anchors pre-provisioned in ECASD<br/>{PK.CI} ⊇ CI1  (SKI = 81:37:0f:51..bebfb, 160-bit)<br/>Own keys: SK.EUICC.ECDSA, CERT.EUICC.ECDSA, CERT.EUM
    Note over S: Holds SK.DPauth.ECDSA and<br/>CERT.DPauth.ECDSA  (issuer = GSMA RSP2 Root CI1)

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over E,L: Phase 1 — ES10b pre-auth material from the eUICC
    L->>E: ES10b.GetEUICCChallenge()
    activate E
    Note over E: sample N_euicc ∈ {0,1}¹²⁸  (16-byte nonce)<br/>retain as pending challenge (anti-replay state)
    E-->>L: euiccChallenge = N_euicc
    deactivate E
    L->>E: ES10b.GetEUICCInfo1()
    activate E
    Note over E: euiccInfo1 = TLV BF20 (55 B)<br/>{svn, euiccCiPKIdListForVerification,<br/>euiccCiPKIdListForSigning}
    E-->>L: euiccInfo1
    deactivate E
    end

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over L,S: Phase 2 — ES9+ InitiateAuthentication over TLS
    L->>S: POST /gsma/rsp2/es9plus/initiateAuthentication<br/>{smdpAddress, euiccChallenge = N_euicc, euiccInfo1}
    activate S
    Note over S: euiccCiPKIdToBeUsed ← (euiccInfo1.verifyList ∩ serverCIs) = CI1<br/>sample N_dp ∈ {0,1}¹²⁸  (serverChallenge)<br/>TID ← fresh transactionId<br/>serverSigned1 = {TID, N_euicc, smdpAddress, N_dp}<br/>serverSignature1 = Sig_SKdpauth(serverSigned1)
    S-->>L: functionExecutionStatus = Executed-Success<br/>{transactionId = TID, serverSigned1 (66–95 B),<br/>serverSignature1, euiccCiPKIdToBeUsed = CI1 (04 14 ‖ 160-bit SKI),<br/>serverCertificate = CERT.DPauth (600–647 B)}
    deactivate S
    end

    rect rgba(128,128,128,0.08)
    Note over E,L: Phase 3 — ES10b AuthenticateServer (eUICC evaluates the server)
    L->>E: ES10b.AuthenticateServer(serverSigned1, serverSignature1,<br/>euiccCiPKIdToBeUsed, serverCertificate,<br/>ctxParams1 = {matchingId, deviceInfo(TAC, capabilities)})
    activate E
    Note over E: V1 = VerifyChain(CERT.DPauth → PK.CI[CI1]) → {0,1}<br/>V2 = Verify(serverSignature1, serverSigned1, PK.DPauth) → {0,1}<br/>V3 = [ serverSigned1.euiccChallenge == N_euicc ]  (freshness)
    alt V1 ∧ V2 ∧ V3 = 1   (OBSERVED: ciTrusted = true, stage = accepted)
        Note over E: sample one-time ECKA keypair (otSK, otPK).EUICC<br/>euiccSigned1 = {TID, smdpAddress, N_dp, euiccInfo2,<br/>ctxParams1, otPK.EUICC}<br/>euiccSignature1 = Sig_SKeuicc(euiccSigned1)
        E-->>L: authenticateServerResponse =<br/>{euiccSigned1, euiccSignature1,<br/>CERT.EUICC.ECDSA, CERT.EUM}
    else V1 ∨ V2 ∨ V3 = 0
        Note over E: abort, emit no key material
        E-->>L: error (invalid CI / signature / stale nonce) → CancelSession
    end
    deactivate E
    end

    Note over L,S: Boundary — CI-trust probe STOPS here.<br/>Full profile download would continue with<br/>ES9+ AuthenticateClient(TID, authenticateServerResponse)
